# Build output.
/site/

# Everything the pipeline needs but nobody should review: the satl/satld pair
# `make gen-fresh` builds, and the scratch tree `make check-gen` regenerates into.
/.cache/

# Python.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NOT ignored, and deliberately so:
#
#   docs/reference/cli/*.md
#   docs/reference/satld.toml.sample
#
# Those are generated by `make gen` and committed anyway. The reason is that a
# reader — or a CI job, or a static host — must be able to build this site with
# no SatL checkout, no Rust toolchain and no FreeBSD. Regenerating on every
# build would make the documentation buildable only where SatL itself is.
#
# The usual cost of committing generated files is that they rot. That is what
# `make check-gen` is for: it regenerates into a scratch directory and diffs,
# so a hand-edit or a moved-on binary fails the build instead of shipping. The
# pages also carry no timestamp, precisely so the diff stays empty when nothing
# has actually changed.

# Deployment. The host, the account, the paths and the runbook: this repository
# is public and none of that belongs in it. `make deploy` reads deploy.conf and
# refuses, with an explanation, when it is absent.
/deploy.conf
/deployment.md
